    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42-a1">

                <pb facs="0082" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg82"/>

                <head>Parliamentary notices.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">House of
                            Lords</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Tuesday</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1861-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 9</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Blackpool and Lytham railroad bill.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">orders of the day</hi>.</p>
                <p>Middleton’s estate.—Standing order No. 141 to be considered, in order to its
                    being dispensed with, on the petition for a private bill.</p>
                <p>Lunacy regulation bill.—Committee.</p>
                <p>Queensland government bill.—Committee.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
